1. What changed

I made a one-line fix in [engine-fast-par-host.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773523384592-10072/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L26): the parallel fast host now calls `App.serializeGraphData(graphOrData)` instead of `App.serializeGraphData()` when it is given a graph instance. This keeps `event-fast-par` bound to the caller’s graph instead of implicitly serializing global app state. `dt` and `event` paths were untouched.

2. Which verification I ran

I ran a focused Node harness that loaded [engine-fast-par-host.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773523384592-10072/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js) with a stubbed `App.serializeGraphData(graph)` and confirmed `new App.EventFastParHost(graph, {})` forwarded the exact graph object (`{"receivedId":123}`).

I also ran `fact-sim-ai` `engine_test` with `action="run"`, `reruns=0`, `strictFinalParity=false`, and `maxWallMs=1` (the tool rejects `0`). Result: `PASS`, `45/45` cases, including `event-fast-par`.

3. Residual risk

The same no-argument serialization pattern still exists in [engine-fast-worker-host.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773523384592-10072/js/app/engine-fast-worker-host.js). I left it unchanged to keep this patch minimal and scoped to the likely `event-fast-par` failure surface.
